&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Coursera + Udemy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera and Udemy are now one company, bringing together two mission-driven brands to create the world’s most powerful platform for turning learning into progress. Together, we help more than 300 million learners and 12,000+ enterprise customers build the skills they need for a world being reshaped by AI. Read more about the combined company by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.coursera.org/coursera-and-udemy-are-now-one-company-creating-the-worlds-most-comprehensive-skills-platform/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is transforming how people learn, work, and grow, and the need for new skills has never been greater. Coursera brings trusted content and credentials from leading university and industry partners, while Udemy brings a dynamic skills marketplace and global network of real-world experts. By combining these strengths, we can connect more people and organizations to the skills they need, when they need them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape what comes next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you’ll have the opportunity to reshape how the world learns and applies skills—and help millions of people participate in the new economy. Bring your ideas, expertise, and perspective to meaningful work that can make a difference at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera + Udemy lets you choose the best way to work, whether it’s from home, an office, or a collaboration space. We’re a globally distributed team that comes together intentionally for collaboration, complex problem-solving, and key milestones — creating opportunities for teams to come together. If you’re ready to make a global impact, help scale unique products across Coursera + Udemy, and grow your career, apply below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue Operations team is seeking a Commissions Analyst to support accurate and timely sales compensation for a global field organization of more than 500 employees. You’ll administer commission plans and payments, maintain data across Xactly Incent, Salesforce Spiff, and Salesforce, and partner with teams across Revenue Operations, Finance, People Operations, and Payroll to resolve issues and improve processes. This role is a great fit for someone who enjoys detailed analytical work and wants to help build reliable, scalable compensation operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About your skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Compensation Administration: &lt;/strong&gt;Supporting commission calculations, incentive payments, plan setup, and employee compensation changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis and Reconciliation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Working with large datasets to validate information, investigate discrepancies, and maintain accurate records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Collaborating with Sales, Revenue Operations, Finance, People Operations, and Payroll to resolve issues and meet deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the end-to-end administration of sales commissions for a global field organization, ensuring variable compensation is calculated and paid accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain sales, quota, and commission data across Xactly Incent, Salesforce Spiff, and Salesforce through regular audits, reconciliations, and data validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate, validate, and track commissions, bonuses, SPIFFs, guarantees, and other incentive payments in accordance with approved plans and policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit monthly and quarterly commissions, investigate discrepancies and root causes, and partner with the appropriate teams to resolve issues before payroll deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compensation-related employee lifecycle changes, including new hires, transfers, promotions, leaves of absence, and terminations. Set up participants, plans, quotas, and assignments in line with approved policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to questions from sales employees and leaders about commission statements, calculations, plan mechanics, and payments, explaining information clearly and protecting confidential data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation and audit trails for calculations, adjustments, exceptions, and approvals to support compensation governance and financial controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve commission processes, controls, reporting, and automation, and support quarterly and year-end close, plan deployment, and quota administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in sales compensation, commission administration, revenue or sales operations, finance, accounting, or a related analytical function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting commission calculations and/or sales compensation plan administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business, Economics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel and/or Google Sheets, including formulas, lookups, pivot tables, reconciliations, and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and ability to work with large, complex datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet monthly and quarterly deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain compensation calculations and plan mechanics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate across teams and handle confidential employee and compensation information with discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Xactly Incent and/or Salesforce Spiff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce and sales opportunity, bookings, and quota data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a global sales organization and multiple compensation plan types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with quotas, attainment, accelerators, crediting, splits, SPIFFs, guarantees, and clawbacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting monthly or quarterly financial close and commission accruals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software/SaaS or education technology; basic SQL knowledge is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This role is available in the following US Pay Zones:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 1: &lt;/strong&gt;$83,600 - $104,500&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 2: &lt;/strong&gt;$79,200 - $99,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 3: &lt;/strong&gt;$73,600 - $92,000&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 4: &lt;/strong&gt;$68,400 - $85,500&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Coursera, we offer competitive, zone-based pay aligned to your location, experience, and role level across four U.S. pay zones. Our total rewards package goes beyond salary, with comprehensive health and wellness benefits, bonus and RSU equity programs, and global perks designed to help you grow and thrive wherever you are.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Pay Zones:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z1: San Francisco Bay Area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z2: NYC and Seattle Metro&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z3: CA, WA, NY, NJ, CO, CT, DC, GA, IL, MA, MD, OR, RI, TX, VA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z4: AK, AZ, DE, FL, HI, ID, IN, IA, KS, KY, MI, MN, MO, MT, NC, NV, NH, OH, OK, PA, SC, TN, UT, VT, WI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Date: &lt;/strong&gt;October 15th, 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Window: &lt;/strong&gt;October 15, 2026 - November 15, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We anticipate the application window will be open until November 15, 2026. Based on business needs, this opportunity may remain posted beyond or close before the anticipated application window.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-NM1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information about how Coursera collects and uses your personal information, please see our &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.clinchtalent.com/1d7f2c0f91ebf75d580f56447fa54859/2acb24eb91f1e23b90ac9e9285de5aaf/Global%20Applicant%20Privacy%20Notice.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coursera + Udemy Global Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect against recruitment fraud, Coursera + Udemy recruiters only communicate via official coursera.org/udemy.com email addresses and never through personal accounts. We do not accept resumes via email or social media; please submit all applications directly through our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you encounter suspicious recruitment activity, please report it via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/Mb8UktwuaJAukb3H7&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Submission Form.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coursera is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a welcoming and inclusive workplace. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to legally protected characteristics and provide reasonable accommodations upon request at recruiting@coursera.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
